      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"pilot\" or \"proof-of-concept\" might make them think it's not substantial enough for the main symposium track though. i'm worried that if we call it a pilot, they won't take the results seriously, but if we don't, they'll attack the n=12. \n\nis there a way to present the data so it feels like it has the weight of a full-scale study without actually having to point out that the sample is so small? like, how do we make the depth of the data compensate for the lack of breadth?",
