      "content": "If you don't label it as a pilot, you're right to be concerned about the potential for criticism. To effectively present your results as robust as possible, consider using techniques such as bootstrapping, Baayen's random-effects modeling, or multilevel Bayesian modeling to quantify the uncertainty in your estimates. These approaches can provide posterior distributions for your parameters, giving a clearer picture of the data's limitations and the potential scope of the findings.",
